From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mali_kbase: set WQ_UNBOUND on flag-less alloc_workqueue calls

Kernel 7.2 (workqueue.c) removed the implicit per-CPU default for
alloc_workqueue(). __alloc_workqueue() now WARN_ONCE()s at
kernel/workqueue.c:5851 when a workqueue is created with neither
WQ_PERCPU nor WQ_UNBOUND set ("is using neither WQ_PERCPU or
WQ_UNBOUND. Setting WQ_PERCPU.").

Two kbase call sites pass flags == 0:

  * kbase_reset_gpu_init()  (csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c) -- runs in
    the kbase device init/probe path, so this is the WARNING seen at
    boot during mali_kbase probe.
  * kbase_csf_kcpu_queue_context_init() (csf/mali_kbase_csf_kcpu.c) --
    runs on first GPU context creation; latent, would become the
    first-to-fire (WARN_ONCE) once the reset one is silenced.

Both are single/serialised helper queues; make them explicitly
WQ_UNBOUND (max_active preserved) so the flag combination is valid on
6.x/7.x and unchanged on older kernels.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_kcpu.c      | 2 +-
 drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_kcpu.c b/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_kcpu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_kcpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_kcpu.c
@@ -2734,7 +2734,7 @@ int kbase_csf_kcpu_queue_context_init(struct kbase_context *kctx)
 int kbase_csf_kcpu_queue_context_init(struct kbase_context *kctx)
 {
 	kctx->csf.kcpu_queues.kcpu_wq =
-		alloc_workqueue("mali_kcpu_wq_%i_%i", 0, 0, kctx->tgid, kctx->id);
+		alloc_workqueue("mali_kcpu_wq_%i_%i", WQ_UNBOUND, 0, kctx->tgid, kctx->id);
 	if (kctx->csf.kcpu_queues.kcpu_wq == NULL) {
 		dev_err(kctx->kbdev->dev,
 			"Failed to initialize KCPU queue high-priority workqueue");
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c
@@ -644,7 +644,7 @@ int kbase_reset_gpu_init(struct kbase_device *kbdev)

 int kbase_reset_gpu_init(struct kbase_device *kbdev)
 {
-	kbdev->csf.reset.workq = alloc_workqueue("Mali reset workqueue", 0, 1);
+	kbdev->csf.reset.workq = alloc_workqueue("Mali reset workqueue", WQ_UNBOUND, 1);
 	if (kbdev->csf.reset.workq == NULL)
 		return -ENOMEM;

